      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "TAUIL Abd Elilah",
        "email": "hafsatauil2004@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-09-02T00:51:48Z"
      },
      "message": "Correct the seam finding: it depends on coverage, not the blend\n\nThe 1.205x gradient excess on the 64 px stride lattice was reported as a general\nproperty of the Hann overlap-add, measured on a single segment. Re-measuring on the\nknown-ink control shows no effect at all (ratio 0.997), and across five segments the\nexcess scales inversely with the supported fraction: 0.925 -> 0.997, 0.723 -> 1.205,\n0.118 -> 1.255.\n\nSo the artifact belongs to partially covered segments, where patches straddle the\ncoverage boundary, not to the blend itself. Adds scripts/repro_seam.py so anyone can\ncheck their own predictions.",
      "tree": {
