      "committer": {
        "name": "TAUIL Abd Elilah",
        "email": "hafsatauil2004@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-08-31T13:53:33Z"
      },
      "message": "PHerc1447 ink survey: control-calibrated negative on four published surface volumes\n\nRuns the 18 August First Letters workflow on prize-eligible PHerc1447 with\nscrollprize/ink_9um, and reports no legible ink across ~42 cm2 and 956 sliding\n4 cm2 windows per direction.\n\nThe negative is calibrated against a 345-window known-ink control (PHerc0139\nw043) run through the identical pipeline, validated against the bucket's own\npublished 2.4um prediction at Pearson r=0.3829 and 2.73x enrichment.\n\nCloses four confounds before the verdict: CT support, label smoothing, voxel\nscale mismatch, and single-region baselines.\n\nAlso documents two defects: one transient remote read aborts the whole ink\ninference, and overlap-blend seams leave a 1.205x gradient excess on the\nstride lattice.",
      "tree": {
